<th id="S4.T2.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Qwen2.5-32B-Chat</th>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">-0.028</td>
<td id="S4.T2.2.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.181</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">End-to-end counterfactual reasoning plausibility alignment on <span id="S4.T2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SoNLI</span>.</span> For each entry, the evaluated model generates supporting and opposing counterfactual justifications, generates likelihoods for each, and produces a plausibility score using the method in Section  <a href="#S4.Ex2" title="4.1 Counterfactual reasoning ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SocialNLI: A Dialogue-Centric Social Inference Dataset" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. We report Pearson correlation <math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> with human scores, and mean absolute error (MAE).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Results ‣ 4.2 Model–Human Alignment ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SocialNLI: A Dialogue-Centric Social Inference Dataset" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows that only GPT-4o, and to some extent GPT-4o-mini, exhibit a meaningful positive correlation with human scores, indicating some ability to separate plausible from implausible inferences. Most other models sit near zero or negative <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, suggesting weak or inverted agreement with annotators. Several models nonetheless post low MAEs by placing scores in a tight band near the dataset mean, most notably Qwen2.5-32B and Llama-3.1-70B, reducing magnitude error without preserving instance-wise ordering. Accordingly, we treat <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> as the primary evaluation signal for <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SoNLI</span> and use MAE as a complementary calibration indicator.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Human-Judged Counterfactuals</h3>

<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this experiment, we rate arguments with human judges, and
address <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">R2</span> by ablating the quality of arguments generated by LLMs and LRMs on <span id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SoNLI</span>. We have humans fact-check model-generated supporting and opposing explanations for each inference (Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Counterfactual reasoning ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SocialNLI: A Dialogue-Centric Social Inference Dataset" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) to see whether the low performance in Section 4.2 was due to poor argument scoring or poor argument generation. We test three LLM-LRM pairs: GPT-4o/o1, Qwen2.5-32B/QwQ-32B, and DeepSeek-V3/DS-R1, on 27 inferences drawn from 9 dialogues (Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Annotating the data ‣ 3 Dataset ‣ SocialNLI: A Dialogue-Centric Social Inference Dataset" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qwen, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI et al., 2025</a></cite>). All inferences and dialogues are verified to have sarcasm or irony.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="445.39" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 633.68 445.39" width="633.68"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,445.39) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(42.52,0) translate(0,41.39) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -42.52 -41.39)"><g class="ltx_nestedsvg" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0) translate(132.8,0) translate(0,41.39)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fg-color:#D9D9D9;" color="#D9D9D9" fill="#D9D9D9" stroke="#D9D9D9" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 394.93 M 205.17 0 L 205.17 394.93 M 410.33 0 L 410.33 394.93"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fill-color:#D9D9D9;--ltx-fg-color:#D9D9D9;" color="#D9D9D9" fill="#D9D9D9" stroke="#D9D9D9" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -90.27 0 L 500.61 0 M -90.27 49.37 L 500.61 49.37 M -90.27 98.73 L 500.61 98.73 M -90.27 148.1 L 500.61 148.1 M -90.27 197.47 L 500.61 197.47 M -90.27 246.83 L 500.61 246.83 M -90.27 296.2 L 500.61 296.2 M -90.27 345.57 L 500.61 345.57 M -90.27 394.93 L 500.61 394.93"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -5.91 L 0 0 M 205.17 -5.91 L 205.17 0 M 410.33 -5.91 L 410.33 0 M 0 400.84 L 0 394.93 M 205.17 400.84 L 205.17 394.93 M 410.33 400.84 L 410.33 394.93"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="0.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -90.27 0 L -84.37 0 M -90.27 49.37 L -84.37 49.37 M -90.27 98.73 L -84.37 98.73 M -90.27 148.1 L -84.37 148.1 M -90.27 197.47 L -84.37 197.47 M -90.27 246.83 L -84.37 246.83 M -90.27 296.2 L -84.37 296.2 M -90.27 345.57 L -84.37 345.57 M -90.27 394.93 L -84.37 394.93 M 500.61 0 L 494.7 0 M 500.61 49.37 L 494.7 49.37 M 500.61 98.73 L 494.7 98.73 M 500.61 148.1 L 494.7 148.1 M 500.61 197.47 L 494.7 197.47 M 500.61 246.83 L 494.7 246.83 M 500.61 296.2 L 494.7 296.2 M 500.61 345.57 L 494.7 345.57 M 500.61 394.93 L 494.7 394.93"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -90.27 0 L -90.27 394.93 L 500.61 394.93 L 500.61 0 L -90.27 0 Z"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -32.43 -33.55)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 22.75)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 10.38)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.69em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="64.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">GPT-4o / </span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 22.76)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_r" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 25.51 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="13.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">o1</span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 157.03 -34.09)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" tran